No RELRO        No canary found   NX disabled   No PIE          No RPATH   No RUNPATH   /home/user/level4/level4

### Vulnerability
- Function `p()`: printf(buffer) with user input (format string vulnerability)
- Allows arbitrary memory reads/writes via format string specifiers

### Target
Write 0x1025544 to 0x8049810 (little-endian: 0x44 0x55 0x02 0x01)

### Exploitation: Byte-by-Byte Writes using %hhn
Use %hhn (1-byte writes) instead of %hn (2-byte writes) to keep payload small:
1. Write 0x44 (68 decimal) to 0x8049810 using %12$hhn
2. Write 0x55 (85 decimal) to 0x8049811 using %13$hhn
3. Write 0x0102 (258 decimal) to 0x8049812 using %14$hn

### Payload Structure (278 bytes total)
```
[12 bytes: 3 addresses at 0x8049810, 0x8049811, 0x8049812]
[56 bytes: padding] > total 68, write %12$hhn
[17 bytes: padding] > total 85, write %13$hhn
[173 bytes: padding] > total 258, write %14$hn
```

### Key Insights
- %hhn writes 1 byte (character count mod 256)
- Character count must increase: 68 < 85 < 258 (no backward jumps)
- Payload fits in 512-byte fgets buffer
- All three writes execute successfully, magic value written, system() triggered

### Acronyms
ELF    Executable and Linkable Format      The standard binary format for executables, object files, and shared libraries on Linux/Unix systems
SSH    Secure Shell                        A cryptographic network protocol for secure remote login and command execution over an unsecured network
NX     No-eXecute                          A memory protection that marks regions (stack, heap) as non-executable, preventing shellcode from running directly in those regions
ASLR   Address Space Layout Randomization  A kernel security feature that randomizes the base addresses of stack, heap, and libraries on each run to make addresses unpredictable
RELRO  RELocation Read-Only                A hardening technique that marks the GOT read-only after startup, preventing GOT overwrites
PIE    Position Independent Executable     A binary compiled to load at a random base address, making it compatible with ASLR for full address randomization

